// Upstream parity checks of the gemma4 chat format (`src/gemma/text/chat.ts`). No GPU.
//
// The fixture `gemma-text/gemma4-chat.json` is generated by an export recipe
// (`tools/export-recipes/gemma4/chat.py`). The expected values come from **calling HF
// `apply_chat_template` independently**, and pass through neither this renderer nor the folding
// of the compiled script (ADR [0084](../../../docs/decisions/0084-gemma-tokenizer-chat.md)
// decision 7 — sharing it would make the parity vacuous).
//
// Six checks:
//
// ① **The rendering** matches the upstream rendering character for character (checked apart from
//    the id sequence, so that when it splits the reader can tell whether the "rendering" or the
//    "encoding" step broke)
// ② **The id sequence** matches `apply_chat_template(tokenize=True)` (the pass line of step 4
//    itself)
// ③ **Out of scope fails loudly** (tools / thinking / tool_call / image parts / unknown role /
//    empty conversation). Ignoring them silently would let "tools were passed but not used" through
//    with no exception, so the rejection paths can only be hit directly
// ④ **The stop-token set** can be derived from the asset's added vocabulary and matches the
//    upstream `generation_config.json` declaration (ADR 0083 decision 8 / 0084 decision 5 — the
//    chat format and the EOS set are the same digest set)
// ⑤ **The turn-local contract of incremental rendering** (`chatTurn`) — the concatenation "the
//    first whole rendering + the generated text + `<turn|>` + the deltas after it" matches, token
//    for token, the whole conversation rendered at once
// ⑥ **Turn cleanup** (`closeChatTurn`) — even when the cleanup fails the serialization slot is
//    returned, and neither the body's failure nor the cleanup's failure is lost (if the slot were
//    not returned, every later `chat` / `dispose` would wait forever)
//
// When the real assets (the distribution's tokenizer, `models/karume-gemma4/`, read through the
// manifest — ADR 0139 decision 1) are present, it also checks that the **full vocabulary** gives
// the same id sequences (the check that closes the gap between the subset and the full one).
// Where they are missing it SKIPs.

import { readTextFile } from "@karume/test-support/fs";
